{
  "_comment": "Curated vertical -> Google Maps SEARCH TERMS + category denylist, shared by EVERY campaign (same role overture_presets.json plays for Overture). source_gmaps.py resolves a vertical here first, then falls back to the overture preset. Lookup strips campaign suffixes, so `clinic-gcc`, `clinic-us` and `clinic-lb` all read the `clinic` entry: ledger ground stays per-campaign, precision is shared, and tuning a vertical once improves every fixture that fires it.\n\nTHREE FIELDS. `terms` is the TIME dial, `keep` is the PRECISION dial, `exclude` is the noise dial.\n  terms   — what a CUSTOMER would type into Maps. Maps is a text search, not a tag filter, so 'emergency plumber' beats the ontology label 'plumbing'. Max 6 (MAX_TERMS_DEFAULT): each term is one query per city, so terms are the time dial.\n  keep    — extra category STEMS that are accepted but NEVER searched, so widening precision costs no time. Stems, not words: 'dermatolog' catches Dermatology AND Dermatologist. This exists because the term-token gate is morphology-naive — measured in Muscat it dropped Dentist (7), Dermatologist (3) and Physical therapist (2), since 'dental', 'dermatology' and 'physiotherapy' are not substrings of what Maps returned.\n  exclude — Maps categories that are real businesses but the WRONG ones. Matched as a lowercase substring against the row's category AND its full categories list. Checked FIRST, so it beats keep: a clinic whose categories include Hospital is still dropped.\n\nHOW THE PRECISION GATE ACTUALLY WORKS (require_category_match, default true): a row is kept when any token >3 chars from any term appears in any of its categories. So `terms` doubles as the allowlist — if a category you WANT is not reachable from some term's tokens, it is dropped. That is why hotel carries 'hostel' and 'lodge': measured in Barcelona, Maps returns Hotel 12, Lodge 2, Hostel 2, and without those terms the last four rows would be discarded.\n\nMEASURED 2026-08-18 (depth 1, one city) — these four are observed, not guessed:\n  trades/plumber, Sydney      Plumber 22/22 (100% on-ICP)\n  salon, Dubai                Beauty salon 16/16 (100%)\n  clinic, Dubai               Medical Center 13, Medical clinic 5, Home health care 1, Hospital 1\n  hotel, Barcelona            Hotel 12, Lodge 2, Hostel 2\n  restaurant, Dubai           Restaurant 8, + cuisine-specific variants (all contain 'restaurant')\n  carservice, Dubai           Auto repair shop 14, Car repair and maintenance 4, Mechanic 2\n  realestate, Dubai           Real estate agent 8, agency 8, consultant 3, commercial 1\n  homeservices, Dubai         Handyman/Handywoman/Handyperson 18, Building restoration 1, Property maintenance 1\n  law, New York               Law firm 9, Personal injury attorney 5, Lawyer 4, Legal services 1\n  property, New York          Property management company 20/20 (100%)\n  staffing, New York          Employment agency 15, Recruiter 3, Temp agency 2\n\nTHREE TERMS EXIST ONLY TO SAVE A MEASURED CATEGORY from the token gate, which ignores tokens of 3 characters or fewer: 'car mechanic' rescues `Mechanic`, 'recruiter' rescues `Recruiter` (the token 'recruitment' is NOT a substring of it), and 'legal services' rescues `Legal services` (note 'law' is 3 chars, so `Law firm` survives only via 'firm'). Add a term whenever a run reports dropping a category you actually want.\nThe rest are reasoned from each fixture's ICP and NOT yet measured. Every run prints the categories it dropped, so tune from that output rather than from this comment.\n\nDELIBERATELY ABSENT: `enterprise` (lb-enterprise). 'The biggest Lebanese companies' is not a Maps category and no search phrase enumerates it; that fixture keeps its existing sources.",
